FDM patch 0003b: the switch's settings are validated, its status values and the midpoint counters
are read-only (session 05, after the independent review of session 04)

Why
  REVIEW-codex-04.md found that the properties patches 0002 and 0003 describe as "counters; the
  simulation never reads them" could be written from outside, and that one of them is not only a
  counter: simulation/integrator/rate/contact-active is compared with the new contact state in every
  step (it decides when a change of scheme is counted and when the multistep history is restarted).
  A write to it could therefore suppress or force a history restart. A negative hold time and an
  unknown release mode were accepted as well.

What it changes (property access only; no arithmetic of any step is touched)
  Read-only now (tied without a setter, exactly as JSBSim ties simulation/sim-time-sec; a write is
  refused by the property system):
    simulation/integrator/rate/contact-active, .../contact-switches
    simulation/integrator/midpoint/steps, newton-iterations, max-newton-iterations, split-steps,
    rounding-exits, euler-fallbacks, not-converged, singular-jacobian
  Validated when written (a refused value throws, and the setting keeps its old value):
    simulation/integrator/rate/rotational-on-contact   -1, 0 to 5, 9 or 10
    simulation/integrator/rate/contact-hold-sec        finite and not negative
    simulation/integrator/rate/contact-release-mode    0 or 1

Why a separate patch and not an edit of 0002 and 0003
  The hashes of 0002 and 0003 are printed in every result file of session 04. They stay as they are;
  this file is applied on top of them.

No switch, and why that is acceptable
  The rule is that a change of JSBSim's physics has a switch that defaults to "unchanged JSBSim".
  This patch changes no physics: the variables, their defaults and every statement of
  FGPropagate::Run are the same. It only replaces "tie the property to the variable" by "tie it to a
  getter (and a checking setter)". Checked the same way as the other patches: bit-identical logs
  with the patches off (tests/native/verify_key.sh patched unpatched,
  tests/native/verify_wasm_patch_off.sh), and the gate reports of c3-ab4 and c2-mid are unchanged
  (REPORT-05, step 1).

